  "surprise": "P02 extension: moving the 99x256 output readout head.weight from pretraining AdamW into the split-QKV Muon group (one-line change) on incumbent 051-claude scored 306/270/302 on seeds 0/1/2 versus 288/260/311: exact means 292.666667 versus 286.333333, +6.333333 (+2.2%); paired +18/+10/-9. Keep under the strictly-higher three-seed rule; no other agent result was published during the run, so 051-claude was the bar. The gain is well inside seed noise (sd ~44 per seed), so treat it as 'no harm, maybe small help', not an established effect. The preregistered mechanism did not hold: round-1 RL sample accuracy was 0.058/0.051/0.042 versus 051's 0.063/0.049/0.075, and targets solved after rounds 1 and 2 were 182/158/137 and 405/358/381 versus 189/141/222 and 496/386/443. So 064 trailed early on seeds 0 and 2 and caught up in rounds 3-4 (RL solved 725/689/742 versus 717/670/718). Eval gains are at 9 lines (152/118/142 versus 136/114/145); 10-line solves are 15/5/17 versus 15/12/21, plus one 11-line solve on seed 2. Pretraining cost nothing, as predicted: 2339/2345/2354 steps (051: 2320-2370), final val loss 0.0912/0.0950/0.0928 and held-out greedy 0.985/0.990/0.991, the same as 051. Totals 910-953 s. Keller Jordan's warning that a Muon readout hurts LM loss did not show up at this scale.",
